<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "independent continuant"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "b is an independent continuant =Def b is a continuant & there is no c such that b specifically depends on c or b generically depends on c"@en .
# 
# http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "spatial region"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "(Elucidation) A spatial region is a continuant entity that is a continuant part of the spatial projection of a portion of spacetime at a given time"@en .
# 
# http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000008
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000008> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
