<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "(Elucidation) p is a process means p is an occurrent that has some temporal proper part and for some time t, p has some material entity as participant"@en .
# 
# http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "disposition"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "(Elucidation) A disposition b is a realizable entity such that if b ceases to exist then its bearer is physically changed & b's realization occurs when and because this bearer is in some special physical circumstances & this realization occurs in virtue of the bearer's physical make-up"@en .
# 
# http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020> .
