<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000888> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "polymer"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000888> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A polymer is a material that consists of many repeated subunits (monomers) to form long chains. The atoms within a polymer chain are bonded together by covalent bonds. The intermolecular forces between polymer chains are typically represented by van der waals forces and hydrogen bonds."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000891
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000891> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000891> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000891> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "disconnected material entity aggregate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000891> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An object aggregate that is a mereological sum of scattered (i.e. spatially separated) material entities, which do not adhere to one another through chemical bonds or physical junctions but, instead, relate to one another merely on grounds of metric proximity. The material entities are separated from one another through space or through other material entities that do not belong to the group."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000896
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000896> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000896> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0023043> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000896> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Druck"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000896> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pressure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000896> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "a quality describing the force exerted per unit area in or on a material."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000896> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "eine intensive Qualität, die die Kraft beschreibt, die pro Flächeneinheit in oder auf ein Material ausgeübt wird."@de .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000899
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000899> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000899> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000833> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000899> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Urformen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000899> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "primary shaping"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000899> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A manufacturing process that creates a defined workpiece from shapeless material by producing cohesion, whereby the characteristic properties of the material become visible in the end product."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000899> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ein Herstellungsprozess, der aus formlosem Stoff durch das Herstellen von Kohäsion ein definiertes Werkstück schafft, wobei die charakteristischen Eigenschaften des Materials im Endprodukt sichtbar werden."@de .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000907
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000907> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000907> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000899> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000907> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Urformen Aus Dem Plastischen Zustand"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000907> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "primary shaping from the plastic state"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000907> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A primary shaping process that involves forming materials from a plastic state."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000907> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ein Urformprozess, der das Formen von Materialien aus einem plastischen Zustand beinhaltet."@de .
